{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Corrected Phase-1 RCA after the failure recurred on 9895-aa2c-8907-4db6.\n\nThe earlier locality-only proposal is stale/incomplete: current main already appends the\nimmediate record-before-next-criterion sentence in primary_criteria_manifest\n(src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py:172-194), yet the real 9895 verifier still\nexhausts with zero banks.\n\nProven root cause: the banking contract is not expressed as an authoritative, finite state\ntransition. RunnerAgentStep concatenates primary_criteria_manifest into ticket_context\n(src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py:220-226), while the completion-verifier system prompt declares\nticket context UNTRUSTED DATA and NEVER instructions\n(src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md:30-37). The authoritative banking text instead\nconditions the write on subjective states such as becoming confident or having sufficient\nevidence and explicitly cautions against cutting evidence short\n(completion_verifier.md:262-279; completion_banking.py:62-75). On a dense criterion the model\ntherefore keeps finding relevant searches without reaching an externally bounded bank transition.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof, pinned to bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 at temperature 0:\n\n- Exact real-ticket baseline through completion.verify_completion, with no sidecar emit or\n  tracker mutation: 24 requests, 38 tools (37 distinct), zero CriterionBank.upsert calls, then\n  CompletionRecoveryError. This reproduces the reported failure.\n- Simple three-criterion disposable-repo control under the unchanged prompt: PASS and 3/3 tool\n  banks. This rules out missing tool wiring, schema incompatibility, and batching alone.\n- Same real 9895 context, changing only authority placement by copying the existing concrete\n  record-before-next directive into the system prompt: PASS and 5/5 tool banks. This confirms\n  the user-context authority contradiction materially suppresses banking.\n- Same real 9895 context, adding an authoritative finite rule (process the current id, use at\n  most three evidence calls, then record MET or fail-closed NOT MET before advancing): PASS and\n  5/5 tool banks. This confirms the missing finite commit transition and rejects simple budget\n  shortage; the unchanged baseline consumed its full budget without progress.\n\nLegitimacy remains defect: completion_recovery.py's module contract and the completion-verifier\nIncremental banking section require each decided criterion to be banked so partial work survives.\nZero-bank exhaustion violates that invariant. Phase 2 should replace the subjective/low-authority\ncontract with the minimal affirmative system-level finite loop, remove imperative wording from\nthe untrusted manifest (leave ids as data), and prove it with a pinned repeated behavioral eval\nplus a simple-ticket negative control."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786264012261835001,"uuid":"42d3be88-ec4c-4710-9bca-3717fa40a63d"}